%description:

Tcp.mss:explicit -- a value of 88 or more is the MSS that the host announces.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the largest segment text that this host sends and announces".

The classes: auto (-1, the default), with a facet for IPv4 and one for IPv6; explicit (88 and
more); invalid (0 to 87, and below -1). The code: TcpConnection::initConnection() and
resolveAddressFamilyMss(). This test separates "explicit" from "auto".

Host under test: host1, the active opener. Observation: level 1, the MSS option of the SYN of
host1 is 536.

%# parameter: Tcp.mss
%# class: explicit
%# value: 536
%# key: *.host1.tcp.mss
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMssExplicit")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return tcpMssOptionOf(context.event.packet) == 536; })
                  .describe("the SYN of host1, with the MSS 536")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMssExplicit compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.mss = 536    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMssExplicit: PASS
